module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "hand_shim_shadows_an_emitted_module" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a hand-authored Rust copy of a .dag module is substituted for the emitted one, and when the emitter evolves the copy silently stops matching both the emitter and the authority** (INVALID STATE: tools.self_host_module_behavioral_transport_roster rows overwrote emitted modules with hand shims -- a shared std-bridge directory (v2_std_node, v2_std_algebra, v2_std_collection, v2_std_diagnostic, v2_std_integer) plus per-row shim lib.rs files -- so the self-host behavioral receipts linked a crate that was neither the emitter's output nor the .dag's meaning. HARM, THREE MEASURED FACES: (1) self_host_03_normalize_behavioral_receipt_holds was red for 13 E0308 because the v2_std_diagnostic shim, last touched in #10929, still spelled Diagnostics as `enum Diagnostics` with `rejected_with_pending(pending: Rc<Diagnostics>, ..)` after the emitter moved the None | Some coproduct to Option<Rc<NonEmptyDiagnostics>>; the red was read as an EMITTER defect (value/Rc boundary at call sites) and briefed as one, while the emitted crate alone cargo-checked clean. (2) The lax v2_std_node shim kept a MALFORMED fixture green: the body_producer driver's Transform body carried zero edges, which v2.std.node behavior_edges_conform refuses (Transform needs count(children) >= 1); against the emitted module the fixture is refused. (3) The same slice hid a hollow ORACLE: the seed's hand-retained v1_compiler::v2_compiler_normalize answered well_formed = true for every tree, and the old fault input (an empty Disj) is accepted by both realizations, so the 03_normalize fault arm was red whichever way emitted normalize behaved -- parity with a stub that accepts everything is not evidence. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the shim is a SECOND realization of a module whose authority is a .dag file, so it is the section 3 fork at the realization layer; nothing ties its bytes to the emitter, so it drifts on every emitter change that touches the module's shape, and it fails in whichever direction the drift points -- toward a compile red that blames the emitter, or toward a laxer check that greens a wrong input. The dissolution trigger the bridge carried ('v2 std self-emits and gunbc emits seed-linked extern imports without hand ABI bridges') had already fired and nothing read it. RECOGNITION RULE: when a witness builds 'the emitted X', read the assembly and ask which bytes of X the emitter actually produced; any file written from the repository over an emitted path is a hand realization and is presumed stale. When a behavioral receipt compares against a hand oracle, run one input the authority REFUSES through both sides before trusting parity. RUNG FOUND AT: silent -- the receipts are outside the required lane, so the red sat on main unnoticed. RUNG NOW, FOR THE ROSTER: structurally impossible -- every shim row was censused (emitted closure builds and the driver passes with no shim), the shims were deleted, and ModuleBehavioralTransportConfig / cssl_seed_linked_behavioral_receipt no longer carry shim_lib_rel or shim_writes, so a row cannot name a shim. CEILING AND RESIDUE: the class survives one layer down, in the seed's other hand-retained oracles (v1_compiler v2_compiler_body_producer, v2_compiler_parse_engine_hooks, v2_compiler_use_site_verdict, v2_compiler_target_carriers, v2_compiler_discovery_enumeration) that the remaining receipts compare against; each is a hand realization that can be laxer than its authority exactly as v2_compiler_normalize was. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the behavioral oracle is the v1 interpreter's evaluation of the SAME .dag entry rather than a hand-retained Rust module, sufficient that no receipt's expected value can come from a copy of the module under test. Replacing one stub with a better stub does not discharge it.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness", decl_name: "cssl_seed_linked_behavioral_receipt", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "tools.self_host_module_behavioral_transport_roster", decl_name: "ModuleBehavioralTransportConfig", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
